@startuml account-lifecycle
title M-UM3: account generation lifecycle (v0 design; v0 range deny; v1 class/enforcement annotations)
hide empty description

[*] --> creating : user.create\n(under the helper lock: allocate UID/GID,\nledger entry, journal)
creating --> active : account, group and home created\n(static range rule already installed; v1 class gates before activation / launch)
state "creation rolled back\n(fresh random 128-bit generation never reused)" as rolled_back
creating --> rolled_back : failure or crash →\nmanager compares OS objects with journal, rolls back
rolled_back --> [*]
active --> active : launch.start (launcher)\nfw.apply (v1)
active --> retiring : user.retire\n(workspace export already recorded or direct operator waiver;\ncommit point: persist retiring)
retiring --> retiring : processes_remain → later retry\ncrash → dependency recovery continues same effect; bounded batches yield lock
retiring --> removed : processes stopped and verified; export obligation discharged;\nhome quarantined;\ndeclared keys destroyed before walk; home deleted;\nonly closed-schema service-generated metadata export; temporary files removed;\naccount and group removed; v1 rules removed last; persist removed
note right of removed: Generation stays in root ledger forever (§4.2).
note left of creating
  [[../spec/helper.md#42-lifecycle Defining spec §4.2]],
  [[../spec/helper.md#43-usercreate §4.3 create]],
  [[../spec/helper.md#46-lock-journal-and-idempotency §4.6 recovery]].
  Root swarma-user-manager owns ledger/cursor, lock, journal, audit.
  OS backend stores account/group records; account owns home content.
  One durable lock protects both binaries; bounded retirement batches yield it.
  Invalid role/ownership/quota refuses before creation (§3).
  All-stop root mark closes create/activation and already-issued create frontier (§8.3).
  Unmanaged name/home and dirty reused UID refuse (§§4.1, 4.3).
  Fresh random 128-bit generation (R-GEN); never reused with UID or label.
end note
note right of active
  Root launcher starts approved executor under agent or qualified workplace UID (§7).
  Workplace untrusted by default; operator act at admission may admit remote worker to trusted circle.
  That enables donor-side opt-ins only; all host boundaries stay, including transfer/review.
  Remote workers stay workplace placements; host loop needs trusted class AND local placement.
  Review-role grant and positive §3 eligibility are separate; circle/class alone is insufficient.
  Helper v1 zero egress, no proxy/loopback or web-service socket; relay/backend publication gate.
  swarma-rb-exec controls run under service principal, never workplace UID.
  Account-wide persistence denial qualifies per OS; idle UID has zero processes.
  swarma-dispatcher service UID owns execution lifetime.
  Broker service UID owns bindings/leases; trusted active agent may be bound.
  Untrusted class never has subscription binding/lease or local agent loop.
  Recorded class + qualified host matrix/ceilings/socket set required.
  Machine-owned exec identity/body pin; drift refuses at launch/retry (§§7-8).
  All-stop mark refuses every physical start, including workspace executors.
  No shared services on hosts admitting untrusted class; v0/Slice 0 refuses it.
  Protected service-class swarma-operator and swarma-observer never host a harness or launch.
  Only configured installer or operator creates them; dispatcher cannot (§4.3).
  Operator SSH: operator device key only; forced operator command; no interactive shell.
  Narrow OS entry/sshd settings remain publication gates (§14 question 17).
  R-NETBIND: no direct/external-http-proxy binding for ANY platform account class.
  One profile-bound listener per bound account generation; only its own proxy.port admitted.
  N15 account_generation/profile_ref/service_generation/served_policy_digest evidence (§8).
  Web default-off; explicit trusted-circle opt-in only (§8).
  Refused launch/stop/fw.apply does not change account state.
end note
note right of retiring
  [[../spec/helper.md#44-userretire Defining spec §4.4]].
  Launcher refuses new starts; broker refuses leases.
  No manager-to-broker call; dispatcher/operator owns unbind obligation.
  Unknown/failed observation does not prove quiescence (§4.7);
  exact retirement observation error: unspecified in spec §4.4.
  TERM/KILL and verification cover the same generation UID set as exec.stop (§4.7).
  Bounded cleanup batches yield shared lock; keep UID/quota reservation and pending evidence.
  Recovery validates shared accounting then requested dependencies, not full unrelated cleanup.
  Root controls quarantine and owns metadata exports; no-follow walks (§6).
  R-TRANSFER: complete result + every blob digest/size-verified and durable outside deletion,
  journaled complete-content receipt before retirement or explicit per-act operator waiver.
  Digest-only/missing/corrupt/unknown evidence keeps deletion closed; dispatcher owns obligation.
  Refusal immutable; bounded new linked repair needs current authority + separate admission.
  Expiry cleanup needs bounded original-admission consent while active; no retiring bypass.
  Security holds remain; standing discard off. Retained content awaits authenticated import
  acknowledgement/authorized release; home retirement need not await import (§7).
  Declared keys destroyed before home deletion.
  Failed/unknown destruction or deletion keeps retiring; unreadable is not absent.
  Retirement metadata export never copies agent-controlled strings/names/links/bodies (§4.4.1).
  Export schema/provenance and audit encoding unpublished (§14 question 6).
  v1 account rules removed AFTER account/group; static range deny remains; no rollback to active.
  Retirement is separate from identity revocation (§4.4).
end note
note "Current: nothing implemented; v0 accounts/launcher/static range deny; v1 narrowing; v2 grants (§13).\nSH2+ joint admission gate I4 remains closed; dispatcher alone invokes the launcher (§§7, 14).\nSeparate explicit swarma-operator home retention: authentication + exact-content confirmation; refused inside agent sessions; confidentiality not guaranteed; format unpublished (§4.4.1)." as Phase
Phase .. retiring
note bottom of removed
  R-OUTCOME: pending stop/retire continues same effect/arguments; terminal result replays.
  R-GEN restore: fence all readers externally; reconcile surviving evidence and epoch floors.
  Never restore retiring/removed to active; lost coverage unavailable, never not_recorded.
  R-TIME: expiry deletion needs boot-inclusive monotonic lifetime, not wall clock alone.
end note
note bottom of creating
  R-RANGE-DENY active test-UID precedence proof at install/start/schedule;
  failure -> incident/readiness drop. Linux every-protocol skuid range; macOS pf + sandbox.
  R-NET-TOOL Linux workplace namespace + Unix-only families; macOS deny-network sandbox + UID deny.
  R-CEILINGS selected Linux non-delegated unit, macOS qualified mechanisms; matrix per OS release.
  Kernel baseline and exact declared socket reachability/deployment inventory qualify (§12).
  R-EXEC full invocation/transitive interpreted inputs qualify; unsupported tools R-VERIFY off-host.
  v0 R-WATCH generation-bound stop/hold/status; no phone/per-account freeze promise.
  v1/S2 freeze lifecycle remains open.
end note
note bottom of retiring
  R-ALLSTOP: manual operator act with authentication + one confirmation; refused in agent sessions.
  Direct same-act service parts; root receiver fence before inventory.
  Receipt-backed account-wide stop; never-launched fresh absence requires full no-launch coverage.
  Unknown/lost history unresolved; no dummy launch or automatic retirement.
  Direct containment/stops progress without dispatcher or other-part acknowledgements;
  lease/renewal freeze, delivered tokens retain vendor lifetime, close delivery/snapshot boards.
  All durable parts, dispatcher included, required before scoped explicit recovery/hold-last.
  Partial/unknown -> incident and closed admission; never automatic restart.
end note
@enduml
